# SEO

## Config

- `src/lib/seo/siteConfig.js` — `VITE_SITE_URL`, page titles/descriptions
- `src/lib/seo/applySeo.js` — updates `document.title` and meta at runtime
- `scripts/generate-seo-assets.mjs` — `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `og-image.png`
- `index.html` — `__SITE_URL__` placeholders replaced at build via Vite plugin

## Runtime

Call `applySeo(tabId)` when suite tab changes (`Dashboard.jsx`) or mode changes (`App.jsx`).

## Build / deploy

```bash
npm run seo:generate   # robots + sitemap + og image
npm run build          # includes icons + seo + vite
```

GitHub Pages: `.github/workflows/deploy-github-pages.yml` (peaceiris → gh-pages). Never re-run obsolete workflow #1 (deploy-pages@v4).

## Rules

- Keep German `lang="de"` and keyword-rich descriptions honest (no stuffing).
- Use `SafeMarkdown` only — never inject SEO text via unsafe HTML.
- After changing public URL, update `VITE_SITE_URL` and re-run `npm run seo:generate`.
- New top-level routes: extend `PAGE_SEO` and sitemap if they become real URLs.
